Third-party data included in src/oce_math_mcp/data/
---------------------------------------------------

nuclides.json.gz is derived from the AME2020 and NUBASE2020 evaluations (files mass.mas20 and
nubase_4.mas20, Atomic Mass Data Center). Values were extracted and converted to JSON; isomer
mass excesses were recomputed as ground state plus excitation energy. The source articles are
published under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/):
  - W.J. Huang, M. Wang, F.G. Kondev, G. Audi, S. Naimi, "The AME2020 atomic mass evaluation (I)",
    Chinese Physics C 45, 030002 (2021), doi:10.1088/1674-1137/abddb0
  - M. Wang, W.J. Huang, F.G. Kondev, G. Audi, S. Naimi, "The AME2020 atomic mass evaluation (II)",
    Chinese Physics C 45, 030003 (2021), doi:10.1088/1674-1137/abddaf
  - F.G. Kondev, M. Wang, W.J. Huang, S. Naimi, G. Audi, "The NUBASE2020 evaluation of nuclear
    physics properties", Chinese Physics C 45, 030001 (2021), doi:10.1088/1674-1137/abddae

src/oce_math_mcp/tools/if97_data.py contains the coefficients of the IAPWS Industrial
Formulation 1997 for the Thermodynamic Properties of Water and Steam (IAPWS-IF97), extracted
from the IAPWS release R7-97(2012), "Revised Release on the IAPWS Industrial Formulation 1997
for the Thermodynamic Properties of Water and Steam", International Association for the
Properties of Water and Steam, https://iapws.org/technical-guidance/release/IF97-Rev .

atomic_weights.json contains the standard and abridged atomic weights published by the IUPAC
Commission on Isotopic Abundances and Atomic Weights (CIAAW), https://www.ciaaw.org/ .
